From: nuubOS Project <noreply@nuubos.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] nuubOS: TV systems fill a square screen, sides cropped

NUUBOS_RA_OVERSCAN_X=<percent> (nuubos-emud: TV systems on a square
handheld screen only, display.conf field 4, default 8): a picture wider
than the screen at full height fills the height as far as at most that
share of its width is cropped, and is scaled to that width beyond; patch
0003 crops the sides evenly. With 8 % (4 % a side) a 4:3
game on the 720x720 RG CubeXX is 783x587 at the top instead of an
integer 2x with large margins (or a 720x540 fit). Not integer scaled.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [nuubOS specific]

--- a/gfx/video_driver.c
+++ b/gfx/video_driver.c
@@ -2410,6 +2410,27 @@
    return true;
 }
 
+/* nuubOS: NUUBOS_RA_OVERSCAN_X=<percent> (set by nuubos-emud for TV
+ * systems on a square handheld screen) fills the height with a picture
+ * wider than the screen as far as at most that share of its width (a
+ * TV's overscan, 8 % by default) is cropped, scaled to fit beyond that: a
+ * 4:3 game on 720x720 at 8 % is 783x587 at the top, its sides cropped
+ * evenly (patch 0003), instead of a small integer 2x or a 720x540 fit.
+ * Not integer: the sharp bilinear or CRT shader keeps the pixels even.
+ * 0 % crops nothing: the override steps aside and normal scaling
+ * (Smart/Underscale/Overscale) decides instead. Returns the share of
+ * the width kept, 0 = off (unset, or 0 %: `pct > 0` here, not `>= 0`,
+ * is what makes 0 % actually step aside instead of forcing a width-fit
+ * that happened to be numerically the same and so masked the bug: it
+ * silently overrode every Integer Scale mode, every time, nuubos-emud
+ * 2026-10-30). */
+static float nuubos_overscan_keep(void)
+{
+   static float keep = -1.0f;
+   if (keep < 0.0f)
+   {
+      const char *s = getenv("NUUBOS_RA_OVERSCAN_X");
+      int pct       = s ? atoi(s) : 0;
+      keep          = (s && pct > 0 && pct < 50) ? 1.0f - pct / 100.0f : 0.0f;
+   }
+   return keep;
+}
+
 /**
  * video_viewport_get_scaled_integer:
  * @vp            : Viewport handle
@@ -2512,7 +2532,20 @@
    /* Make sure that we don't get 0x scale ... */
    else if (width >= content_width && height >= content_height)
    {
-      if (keep_aspect)
+      unsigned nuubos_w = (unsigned)roundf(height * aspect_ratio);
+
+      if (keep_aspect && nuubos_overscan_keep() > 0.0f && nuubos_w > width)
+      {
+         unsigned nuubos_h = height;
+         if (nuubos_w * nuubos_overscan_keep() > width)
+         {
+            nuubos_w = (unsigned)roundf(width / nuubos_overscan_keep());
+            nuubos_h = (unsigned)roundf(nuubos_w / aspect_ratio);
+         }
+         padding_x = (int)width  - (int)nuubos_w;
+         padding_y = (int)height - (int)nuubos_h;
+      }
+      else if (keep_aspect)
       {
          int8_t half_w       = 0;
          int8_t half_h       = 0;
